On the credit card thing:   (in case nobody else answered already)

Rumor:  "Shopkeepers accept credit cards, as long as you pay cash."

Any regular credit card (this includes the much-aclaimed PYEC*) _cannot_
be used to pay shopkeepers.  Credit cards do not have charges.  (Maybe
in a future version this might be implemented...  But not yet.  The pros
and cons and ex-cons of this were debated earlier this summer here...)

Why have a credit card if you can't use it on a spending spree, you ask?
Why, to unlock doors and chests, of course.  It's lighter to carry than
a lockpick.  Of course, you can't use it to lock things back up again.
(It's safer and quieter** than kicking doors and chests open.)

