To elaborate, uncursed scrolls of charging will add one charge to
the item being charged.  Blessed scrolls of charging will charge
an item to its max or initial charge status, I'm not sure which.
For magic markers the numbers are different(but thats another thread).
Also, wands and magic markers may only be charged once; I'm not sure
about other chargable items...

The only other way to charge items is to #invoke the PYEC.  It is
the Tourist quest item, and only neural characters may use it.  (It
has other abilites too).  I believe the uncursed/blessed status of
the PYEC has the same effect as the u/b status of scrolls of charging.

